# Retained results for the no-four-MUBs programme

This is a library of established statements, not a list of research targets.
**No result here excludes a fourth MUB globally.** Each folder states its
hypotheses. Anything that relies on the accepted reconstruction inputs
([ASSUMPTIONS.md](../MinimalConstruction/ASSUMPTIONS.md)) says so.

Throughout, a *quartet edge* is a transition matrix between two bases of a
hypothetical set of four MUBs. The published Fourier-family and Tao
exclusions cited below are [Jaming et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/0902.0882)
and [Brierley–Weigert](https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.4051).

## Single transitions (every quartet edge)

Campaign bookkeeping: [enlarged branch-cell coverage](CampaignLayerCoverage/README.md)
provides an exact rational split audit with a registered verifier. It is
not a claim that the branch layer is closed.

| Result | What is established | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| [Balanced products](BalancedProducts/BalancedFourSeedIdentity.md) | Every balanced three-row product sum, and its column analogue, vanishes for every non-Tao Hadamard | Under the accepted reconstruction inputs |
| [F3 blocks](FourierBlocks/FourierBlockClassification.md) | A 3×3 Hadamard block forces the Fourier family, its transpose, or Tao | Unconditional structural theorem |
| [Edge rigidity](EdgeRigidity/README.md) | Zero 3×3 minor ⇔ antipodal quotient ⇔ F3 block. Hence **no quartet edge has a zero 3×3 minor** ([corollary](EdgeRigidity/QuartetEdgeCorollary.md)). Other lemmas: a three-valued quotient forces Tao or an antipodal pair; three-row projector rank 5; one binary direction forces a zero minor; balanced rank exactly 3; cubic incidence C*C ≤ 18I; the Karlsson pairing detector; Cauchy–Binet corner-slack identities | Mostly unconditional. The balanced-based items inherit the reconstruction inputs. The quartet corollary uses the published Fourier exclusion |
| [Tao exclusion](ExceptionalEndpoints/Tao/README.md) | Tao has exactly 90 common rays and no orthogonal pair of them, so it lies in no MUB triple and hence in no quartet | An independent replacement for the citation. The elimination step is frozen msolve output, which Singular reproduces but which is not certified |
| [Frame potential](SpectralMoments/FramePotential.md) | Φ₃ = (9/2)Φ₂ − 1296 + 9B, and Φ₂ ≥ 336 for non-Tao Hadamards | The bound uses balanced products |
| [Fourier neighbourhood (D2)](FourierNeighbourhood/README.md) | If a transition lies within 1/1024 of the F6 orbit, no 4+1 configuration exists. Hence every quartet edge has d_F > 1/1024 | Exact integer-interval certificate with 389,672 leaves and no dependencies. It excludes carriers outside every published family, but only over a tiny radius |
| [Fourier seed atlas (T2 progress)](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedAtlas/README.md) | Every Fourier-family corner seed lies on an explicit union of 12 surfaces and 36 R=0 curves; exact seed distances and direct carrier-tube transfer bounds | Unconditional identities and exhaustive exact enumeration. Exclusion radii are in the tube rows and inverse seed-to-carrier estimates in the lift rows below |
| [Uniform Fourier matrix tube](FourierNeighbourhood/PracticalTube/README.md) | Every quartet edge has d_Four>1/16384, uniformly over the family, transpose and equivalences | Unconditional computer-assisted theorem: 294 covering leaves, 2,178,035 candidate six-cliques, exact reduction audit and 408 positive controls. Seed lifting remains separate |
| [Uniform Fourier tube and seed obstruction](FourierNeighbourhood/UniformTube/README.md) | Every quartet edge has d_Four > 2^(−2^590). An exact atlas seed has d_Four(H₊/√6) > 1/40, disproving unrestricted seed lifting | Historical radius uses two published theorems; superseded by PracticalTube. Counterexample uses accepted local reconstruction identities and lies outside D₀; D₀-restricted lifting remains open |
| [Exact D₀ Fourier-atlas rigidity](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/ATLAS_RIGIDITY.md) | An exact atlas seed which is maximal and has 0<R≤20 has only Fourier-family carriers, including the transpose. Also an explicit three-block completion bound | Unconditional physical-matrix statement; exact six-corner identity and 19-node rational Bernstein certificate. Positive-radius lifts: see the lift rows below |
| [Conservative D₀ seed lifting](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/CONSERVATIVE_LIFT.md) | Explicit R-separated seed-to-carrier bound and whole-cell exclusion; a nonvacuous phase cube of half-width 10^(-19) is certified | Uses accepted strict reconstruction inputs and the new exact mean/squared-gap certificates. Constants are not production-scale. R=0 crossings are handled locally by the R=0 lift and the production cube below |
| [Direct D₀ seed lifting](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/DIRECT_LIFT.md) | A strict alternative-side corner gap gives d_Four≤L ε. A patch with L<189, transverse half-width 2×10⁻⁷ and tangential half-width π/512 is certified | Uses accepted strict reconstruction inputs; all physical starting branches covered by the criterion. Transverse production width open; R=0 crossings are handled locally by the R=0 lift and the production cube below |
| [Small-R obstruction to the present tube](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/SMALL_R_OBSTRUCTION.md) | A D₀∩F carrier has R<1/200 but d_Four>1/16000. Another has maximal R<18 and d_Four>1/300 | Accepted reconstruction inputs; all 400 corners and minors checked per example. Refutes pairing δ=1/16384 with m≥1/200, not quartet exclusion |
| [Larger F6 quartet tube](FourierNeighbourhood/ClusterTube/README.md) | No quartet edge lies within projector distance 1/30 of the F6 monomial orbit | Unconditional integer common-ray cover and exact sharp-angle graph. Local to F6; the family-wide radius remains 1/16384 |
| [Production-width D₀ seed cube](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/PRODUCTION_CUBE.md) | Full phase cube of half-width π/512 at (4π/3,5π/3,0,π), with R<1/5, excludes every physical maximal carrier as a quartet edge, including R=0 | Unconditional physical theorem; complete 227-leaf partition, 96/160-bit certificates, and fast 72-frame rule. Uniform whole-family lifting and T1′ cutoff remain open |
| [Continuous small-R and zero-atlas neighbourhoods](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/ZERO_NEIGHBOURHOOD.md) | Radius π/4096 along a genuine maximal Fourier curve to δ=π/128, R<1/2; trimmed zero-atlas arcs and three further production cubes excluded from D₀ | Unconditional; 13 extension cubes, complete 740-box arc partition, independent 96/160 verification and fast containment. Explicit near-grid gaps remain; no new containment on the 53-cell benchmark |
| [All F6 corner neighbourhoods](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/NEAR_F6_CLOSURE.md) and [analytic extension](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/EXTENDED_ANALYTIC_RADII.md) | All six classes covered; the extension gives uniform seed radius 2⁻⁴⁵ and radius 2⁻⁴⁶ around Fourier reference seeds with M≤2⁻⁸⁶ | Unconditional physical theorem, including R=0. The extension enlarges the F3 and rank-one cubes eightfold, with exact algebra and 160/256-bit cap checks. Constants remain very small; intervening atlas shoulders and practical whole-family lifting remain open |
| [Exact Fourier maximum R](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/FOURIER_MAX_R.md) | Complete 400-corner formula; exactly twelve zero-maximum parameter points, all F6. For M≤36, d_F6≤π√M/144 and reference exclusion radius 1/30−π√M/144, both orientations | Exact two-way Laurent census and analytic phase-gauge proof. A bound on explicit Fourier references, not an off-family seed lift or universal T1′ cutoff |
| [Completion-error seed lift](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/RESIDUAL_LIFT.md) | Fixed-reference inverse estimate gives a non-F6 cube of half-width 1/2000, 8<R<9, carrier distance <1/50 | Unconditional physical theorem; complete side covers, two precision replays and independent physical/permutation controls. Production width and uniform seed scope remain open |
| [Regional Fourier matrix tubes](FourierNeighbourhood/WideFamilyTube/README.md) | Radius 1/256 on 191 closed family-parameter boxes, with 1/128 on four; direct radii 1/96 and 1/48 | Unconditional integer covers and exact graphs; 79 coarse boxes have no new certificate. Uniform whole-family radius stays 1/16384 |
| [Regional D₀ seed lift](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/REGIONAL_SEED_LIFT.md) | Half-width 1/10000 at an explicit non-F6 Fourier seed gives distance <1/50 into a proved 1/48 tube; 8<R<9 | Unconditional physical theorem, complete side covers and exact 400-corner nonvacuity. Production width and uniform seed scope remain open |
| [Larger matched-cover seed lift](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/MATCHED_COVER_LIFT.md) | One F6 seed cube has half-width 1/512, with two additional classes at 1/1024 and 1/2048; all enter the 1/36 F6 tube | Unconditional physical theorem; 255-leaf exact seed cover and two precision replays. Production width and whole-family scope remain open |
| [Local D₀ lift across R=0](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/R_ZERO_LIFT.md) | Phase half-width 1/2048 around one F6 seed implies normalized Frobenius distance <1/40 and hence quartet exclusion | Unconditional physical theorem; complete side matching at two precisions. Both signs of R and strict D₀ points occur; full production width and whole-family scope remain open |
| [Movable Fourier references](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/MOVING_REFERENCE.md) | The residual whole-cell lifting criterion may use any rational Fourier parameters, with a reference chosen per leaf of a complete seed partition and the regional radii where proved | Exact matrix identities; [receipt](../Verification/T2_moving_reference_2026-09-29/certificate.json). A criterion, not a claim that it succeeds on every box. Its check `verify_moving_reference.py` is not yet registered in the root verify.py |
| [Paired side prune](CornerBounds/PairedSidePrune/README.md) | Joint row/column necessary identities and fractional R bounds exclude 4/53 retained production boxes from D₀ | Unconditional, division-free, exhaustive finite covers; 49 unresolved and no change to the live driver |
| [Measured campaign second pass](CornerBounds/CampaignSecondPass/README.md) | **93/512 whole held-out enlarged survivor cells excluded (18.2%)**, 1.84 local CPU-s per input; separate R-gap certificates on 56/202 D₀-touching cells | Complete bounded seed covers, original-baseline recheck, all accepted results replayed at 160 bits. Standalone batch command; no full-campaign or high-R runtime saving claimed |
| [Strict Fourier-side completion](FourierNeighbourhood/SeedLifting/FOURIER_SIDE_COMPLETION.md) | A strict E₂(z,w) seed with side B_F has the unique full carrier N(z,w), up to the remaining row phases/permutations | Unconditional row-mean classification; all eight signed-equilateral exceptions have R=0. Identifies the endpoint parameters for local tube tests |
| [Corner boundary bounds (T1)](CornerBounds/README.md) | A qualitative gap away from F6 seeds; exact positive-sheet Fourier-family curve in D₀ ∩ F disproves the proposed m ≥ 20, η ≤ 0.05. Also an unconditional square identity proving all physical corner R values nonnegative | The gap uses accepted strict-corner coverage; the H₊ identification uses local side identities. No explicit sufficient threshold or new prune |
| [Side-column prune (T1 progress)](CornerBounds/SideColumnPrune/README.md) | A two-phase cover excludes seed boxes from D₀ without constructing H₊; four level-9 cells retained as singular by the existing tests are certified out | Uses only physical flatness/orthogonality and outward interval arithmetic. Standalone general pruning function; superseded in production by the side-triple prune |
| [Side-triple prune (stronger T1 tool)](CornerBounds/SideTriplePrune/README.md) | Surviving column labels must form a compatible triple with the prescribed Gram matrix. Excludes all eleven retained local branch cells, seven beyond the single-column prune | Division-free adjugate and remaining-column identities; graph includes loops/repetitions and is valid at singular Grams. No reconstruction inputs. **In production: excludes 95.6% of the 14.0M campaign branch-layer cells** |
| [Regular implicit side charts (T6)](RegularSideCharts/README.md) | Every physical R>0 side has an analytic local chart, det(J)²=R/64, with quantitative bounds and an outward validator. Six cited T6 cells cross R=0; one is strictly positive | Unconditional side theorem; full H₊ branch matching remains conditional. No complete T6 or quartet certificate |
| [T6 residual cells](RegularSideCharts/ResidualCells/README.md) | On four full benchmark cells, D₀ implies R>1. The positive cell has a complete 61-chart reconstruction atlas with exact coverage audit | Local gap is unconditional for physical maximal corners. Atlas uses existing reconstruction inputs; bounds can be broad. No whole-cell quartet exclusion |

## Common unbiased rays of a pair

| Result | What is established | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| [Finite common-ray algebra](CommonRays/FiniteCommonRayAlgebra.md) | With all 3×3 minors nonzero and m zero 2×2 minors: a complete intersection of length 252−2m, and a Gorenstein quotient of length 180−2m holding every physical ray. So there are at most 180−2m common rays, and m ≤ 45 | Analytic. Applies on quartet edges by EdgeRigidity |
| [Cluster cover](CommonRays/ClusterCover/README.md) | Capacity-one ray clusters give a quartet certificate without root counting or nondegeneracy. Excludes an explicit seed cube of radius 1/1024 near the campaign's X₆ example; the automatic campaign version certifies production cells (X₆ and g3 cubes at campaign size included) | Analytic theorem plus interval replay using accepted local reconstruction identities and campaign Taylor models. **This is the campaign's certificate** |
| Cover acceleration: [Cartesian exclusion](CommonRays/ClusterCover/CARTESIAN_EXCLUSION.md), [sharp capacity](CommonRays/ClusterCover/SHARP_CAPACITY.md), [label refinement](CommonRays/ClusterCover/LABEL_REFINEMENT.md) ([receipt](../Verification/Campaign_cartesian_cover_2026-09-29/README.md)) | Partitioned labels and tighter interval overlaps certify 12 retained difficult cells in 132 rather than 647 local CPU-s; g3 certifies at radius 0.005 without external splitting. Also proves the exact cubic capacity threshold ½ arccos(1/4) | Written interval/label proofs, paired whole-cell runs and positive controls. **Now the campaign's production method** (cover only): an unbiased 0.2% campaign sample certified 17,291 of 17,291 cells at 25 s mean ([report](../NumericalCampaign/Campaign/cluster/REPORT_2026-09-29b.md)) |
| [Rank and spectral conditions](CommonRays/RankSpectralConditions.md) | A quartet forces rank[Γ₀…Γ₄] ≤ 168−2m and Q₆ = det(6I−B_w) = 0 | Necessary conditions only |
| [Phase collisions](CommonRays/PhaseCollisions.md), [two-valued anchor](CommonRays/TwoValuedAnchor.md) | In any MUB triple, no mixed column quotient takes one value 4 or more times, and each takes at least 3 values | Unconditional |
| [One-phase recovery](CommonRays/OnePhaseRecovery.md) | One relative phase is always a rational function of the data (rank 2) | Unconditional |
| [Two-rectangle alignment](CommonRays/TwoRectangleAlignment.md), [completion substitution](CommonRays/CompletionSubstitution.md) | Coefficient rank lies in {4,5,6}; rank 6 has no solution and rank 4 is excluded; at most 6 alignments per placement | Strict rectangles; rank 5 open |
| [No affine phase orbits](RelativePhases/PhaseGaugeObstruction.md) | No nonconstant affine phase orbit of a common-unbiased ray | Every order-six Hadamard |

## Triples and relative phases

| Result | What is established | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| [Relative-phase compatibility](RelativePhases/RelativePhaseCompatibility.md) | Exact kernel/quadratic recovery; Tr(W³) ≤ 120 on Tr(W²) = 30 | All Hadamard pairs |
| [Quadratic phase cone](RelativePhases/QuadraticPhaseCone.md) | The phase cone is cut out by W(A) = 0; exact coupling system for three Hadamards; decision for kernel dimension ≤ 2; the 35/78 SOS bound | Addendum to the above |
| [Matching forms](Triples/MatchingForms.md) | A matching is the factorisation D_I(η) = D_U(r)D_V(s), and the trivial one is infinitesimally isolated. There is a residual-tensor criterion for a second matching. **Lemma Z:** every Zauner triple has count ≥ 2 | Unconditional; Lemma Z is checked exactly |
| [Triangle nullities](Triples/TriangleNullities.md) | The number of diagonal-phase matchings of any MUB triple is 0, 1, 2 or 6; three force six; the moduli space is disconnected | Unconditional. Whether count 1 occurs is open |
| [Three-row Gram](Triples/README.md) | S ≥ 126 (SOS), with strict inequality on quartet edges; sharp defect bound 4/17 | One supplied step independently re-read |
| [Simultaneous reconstruction](RelativePhases/SimultaneousReconstruction.md) | How the carrier is used without discarding relative phases | Bookkeeping |

## Toward a fourth basis

| Result | What is established | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| [Covariance contraction](Triples/CovarianceContraction.md) | J ⪯ 3I and tr J² ≤ 60, and **a fourth basis exists iff tr J² = 60** | One-scalar reformulation |
| [Completion and imbalance](Completion/CRITERION.md) | Bloch rank 2 or 3; a flat two-ray completion is unique if it exists; exact imbalance formula | All carriers |
| [Four-basis chirality](FourthBasis/Chirality/README.md) | A rank-2 plane splits into two common rays iff e₃(G) = 2Σc² = 0; the fourth basis is assembled from three planes | Unconditional |
| [Flat complement](FourthBasis/FlatComplement/README.md) | Three strict columns of a fourth basis determine the other three; at most 4 flat complement rays | Unconditional |
| [4+1 reduction](FourthBasis/FourPlusOne/README.md) | Constant five-ray Gram with a rank-one defect linear in the seed; degree-2 moment barrier; ghost gap \|F\|² ≥ 54 | 20-moment count only on strict a = −1 |
| [Anchor inequalities](AnchorInequalities/README.md), [aligned-anchor elimination](AnchorElimination/SmallAnchorElimination.md) | Three necessary coefficient inequalities; exact anchor decision for a fixed aligned quartet | Exclusions are local only |
| [Ghost factors](FourthBasis/GhostFactors/README.md) | Laurent ghosts block equality-only elimination; 36 quadratic factors remove them without losing physical rays | Unconditional tool |
| [Sheet conjugation](Sheets/README.md) | H₋(ā,b̄,c̄,d̄) ≅ conj H₊(a,b,c,d); excluding one sheet over a conjugation-closed region suffices | Analytic |
| [Side branch lemma (T4)](Sheets/BRANCH_LEMMA.md) | Regular side-root changes permute only the last three columns or rows; continued branches are valid across dF = 0 | Exact algebra, using accepted sign-selected side identities; the alternative δ chart is undefined at s = 0 |

## Quartet faces

| Result | What is established | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| [Count two](Quartets/CountTwo/README.md) | A triangle with exactly two matchings has a zero-minor edge, so no quartet face has count 2 | Unconditional; the quartet use goes through QuartetEdgeCorollary |
| [Count six](Quartets/CountSix/README.md) | A quartet has 0, 1 or 3 count-six faces | Uses QuartetEdgeCorollary |

**Together:** every quartet face has count 1 or 6, and some face has count
1. No four MUBs ⇐ **N1** (no count-one triple without zero minors); see
[Quartets](Quartets/README.md). N1 is open. The direct attack is archived at
`../NoFourMUBSArchive/N1-attack-2026-09-27/`. The current route, a
certified quartet exclusion that bypasses N1, is
[NumericalCampaign](../NumericalCampaign/README.md).

## Barriers

[BARRIERS.md](BARRIERS.md) lists proved counterexamples and feasible
relaxations that rule out tempting shortcuts. It also lists the archive's
"accepted" inputs that were never proved and must not be used.

Each statement has its proof next to its verifier. The root verify.py
replays all registered checks in an isolated copy; the latest complete run
is [Verification/root_run_2026-09-29](../Verification/root_run_2026-09-29/summary.json).
The cluster-cover checks also require the pinned campaign Julia environment.

Some provenance notes cite paths such as `KarlssonAndMeasurements/…` or
`work/…`. Those exist only in the archived snapshot
`../NoFourMUBSArchive/NoFourMUBS-before-seven-MUB-audit-20260922-200735.zip`
and are history, not dependencies.
